node_modules

# .env.local is listed here but IS deliberately tracked in git — `.gitignore`
# does not untrack a file that was already committed, and in this case that is
# the behaviour we want. Everything in it is Firebase *web client* config plus a
# reCAPTCHA *site* key, all of which are public by design and already ship
# inside the browser bundle; per Firebase's own docs these "are ok to include in
# code or checked-in config files". Access control here is firestore.rules, not
# secrecy of the API key.
#
# Do NOT "fix" this by deleting the file. deploy.yml also passes the same values
# in from repo secrets, and real environment variables take precedence over
# .env files in Vite — so the committed file is the fallback that keeps a deploy
# working if a secret is ever missing or renamed. Removing it would turn that
# into a silently broken production bundle, because the config is only read at
# runtime in the browser and nothing fails at build time without it.
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Dry-run output of scripts/migrate-team-planner.mjs — a full copy of the
# spreadsheet's contents, regenerated on every run.
scripts/team-planner-migration-preview.json
